[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says its reports are one bug with one fix queued. Read by body, not by
subject, they are three problems. Each now has a ticket of its own.

#4471 closed on 5 October. Engineering fixed the parser (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`)
and won't fix the hint: the booking-v3 form is retired.

<Callout kind="warn">
The one-day reports are still open. Neither the parser fix nor retiring the form touches them.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<SplitTable ticket={4471} />

## How to tell them apart

- **Parser.** Day and month swapped, from a tenant that writes the day first, through the app,
  email or a booking-v2 form.
- **Hint.** Day and month swapped too, but only through the booking-v3 form, which tells people to
  type the month first. Same symptom as the parser, different fix.
- **One day.** The date moves by a single day, or differs between two time zones. Not a swap. The
  desk already lists these in its notes and counts them under the parser, by tenant.

## How they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line and nobody reads
the body. These reports don't share one subject line. [Triage](/kb/triage/dedupe) says to merge when unsure. The intake tag is
guessed from the reporter's browser, not the tenant.

## Lessons

- A big ticket can be several bugs with one symptom. Read the bodies before you call it known.
- Count by cause, not by subject.

